Perform a complete integration and balancing pass on the improved EnemyAI. Do not add major new
  features unless required to fix a verified problem.

  Review the interactions among:

  - Strategic state transitions
  - Target scoring and target commitment
  - Archer kiting and tactical positioning
  - Swordsman screening
  - Rallying and attack waves
  - Base defense and unit recall
  - Strategic production
  - Essence management
  - Unit death and squad cleanup
  - Victory and defeat handling

  Look for emergent problems such as:

  - Units oscillating between commands or targets
  - Archers retreating forever
  - Swordsmen failing to reach combat
  - Squads waiting indefinitely
  - Attacks fragmenting into single-unit streams
  - The AI remaining permanently defensive
  - Distant attackers repeatedly being recalled
  - Production deadlocks
  - Hidden-information cheating
  - Frame-rate-dependent decisions
  - Dead units remaining in AI data structures

  Create or extend automated regression tests for every issue found. Add a deterministic headless
  simulation harness if one does not already exist. Run multiple fixed-seed matches or scenario
  simulations and report useful measurements, including:

  - Time of first attack wave
  - Number and composition of waves
  - Defensive state frequency
  - Units produced by type
  - Essence left unspent
  - State transition counts
  - Any stalled units or invalid targets
  - Match outcome and approximate duration where practical

  Tune named AI configuration values conservatively. Preserve player controls, fog of war, visuals,
  economy values, unit statistics, and core victory conditions.

  After implementation:

  1. Run the complete automated test suite.
  2. Run a syntax or compilation check.
  3. Run all deterministic simulations and report their results.
  4. Launch the game and perform a full manual gameplay smoke test.
  5. Verify menu, pause, restart, selection, recruitment, camera, fog, combat, victory, and defeat
  behavior.
  6. Take screenshots only under /work/screenshots, inspect every screenshot with view_image, and report
  all visual problems.
  7. Clearly distinguish verified behavior from subjective balance observations.
  8. List any remaining limitations or recommended follow-up work.

  Do not commit changes.

  This sequence keeps each change independently testable and makes regressions easier to locate. The
  final prompt then validates the AI as one integrated system rather than assuming individually correct
  features will automatically work well together.
